==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{proto|petwōr|title=Common Germanic|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kwetwōr|lang=ang}}.

Common Germanic cognates include Old High German [[fior]] (German ''[[vier]]''), Old Saxon [[fiuwar]] (Dutch ''[[vier]]''), Old Norse ''[[fjórir]]'', Gothic [[𐍆𐌹𐌳𐍅𐍉𐍂]].

IE cognates include {{proto|Slavic|četiri|title=Common Slavic|lang=}} (Russian [[четыре]]), Old Irish [[cethair]], Greek ''[[τέσσαρες]]'', Latin ''[[quattuor]]''.

